{"step_index":56,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T22:45:00Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-17T04:15:00+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-17T04:15:04+05:30\nThe search for \"\"popup\" animation \"moviepy\" python github\" returned the following summary:\nTo create a \"popup\" animation in **MoviePy**, you typically control the scaling or positioning of an object (like an image or text) over time using lambda functions[1][2]. Since MoviePy does not have a built-in \"popup\" effect, you must define the animation logic by manipulating the clip's properties dynamically[3].\n\n### How to Create a Popup Animation\nYou can achieve a \"pop\" effect by scaling the clip from size 0 to 1 over a short duration[1][2].\n\n#### Basic Logic\n1.  **Define a resizing function:** Use the `.resize()` method with a function of time `t` to simulate the scale increasing[4][2].\n2.  **Compose the clip:** Use `CompositeVideoClip` to overlay your animated element onto the main video[1][5].\n3.  **Set the duration:** Ensure the animation clip has a defined start and duration[6].\n\n#### Example Snippet\n```python\nfrom moviepy.editor import VideoFileClip, ImageClip, CompositeVideoClip\n\n# Load your video\nvideo = VideoFileClip(\"background.mp4\")\n\n# Load the popup image\npopup = ImageClip(\"popup.png\").set_duration(2)\n\n# Create a popup effect: scales from 0 to 1 in the first 0.5 seconds\n# 't' is the time within the clip\npopup = popup.resize(lambda t: min(1, t * 2)) \n\n# Set position and overlay\npopup = popup.set_position(\"center\")\nresult = CompositeVideoClip([video, popup])\n\nresult.write_videofile(\"output.mp4\")\n```\n\n### Key Techniques for Animations\n*   **Scaling:** Use `.resize(lambda t: ...)` to create zoom-in or \"pop\" effects[4][2].\n*   **Positioning:** Use `.set_pos(lambda t: ...)` to move objects across the screen[1][2].\n*   **Custom Effects:** If you need complex transitions, you can define a custom function using `.fl()` (frame-loop) to transform pixels directly, though this is more advanced[4][6].\n*   **GitHub Resources:** \n    *   The [official MoviePy GitHub repository](https://github.com/Zulko/moviepy) is the primary place to check for updates and documentation[7][5].\n    *   Search the [MoviePy Discussions](https://github.com/Zulko/moviepy/discussions) for community-shared transition scripts and effects[3][8].\n\nFor more complex animations like professional motion graphics, developers often use the `fl` method to apply custom mathematical functions to the frame transformations[4][6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHPYfiEewrioHPWU0znyoZFnMZDdk4wL74XfEgVn0g_uxikqpEXJM7yZNa3IVtSAydfMvzfWPD3pHrGVYd6ex2VnVNr9mCt_MlSEPH50T93nRrGc-NtQ5dzMneslFHpOsGSnlYWsJlZuLVS0bpu2-i1aR9-Q8J0zw==)\n[2] [youtube.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGcGhoGvCVtzBV1IWCf8DQI6ua2H0Feqec_4C5hflhQf_VvPR7ll4TZqJFLEkvrdQlKrPJYMg64mJC0mSd-zPYSvak-T4zgdPhkH6s_Ihx-ksyQ5TRGzGdlviYALg2tPDo=)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF1aTPZSP7qsk7qWVw5ZQ3mpd_PKxCLea-bV1w9jZ6svfUxSPyrEAy1NVAerc5YDTSqDTaQtxAwcMGxjrJGMt6rV3yy3U5gMieoKyb-DSGvNLLVyoZsfwwx24z3muEtyefcMwJ9YAo=)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHXtpfLUYrYcx6lEIAa44r8oyhTSZfE2KQJtPH-M1EI19yRdVY76W9zyH0pzjhT9xgJa78Lz0GmF8eyJlcvlQ2Ynu-MsLIwX9BMcl5AewilehhzRB1pGEK-Js1pUoxqlv5K)\n[5] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEx9rw5PxjxeDAHtwHPGlqiB4hiq3bSls5MC_Dh9B0bbeuFO1sh6RkrfXtj39KtyGfQLTDaEQr80i5mZqdGHk-5xg1R6G7dIzVLZlGOXmrTkdRCRobYW6jbN7OAqhF2ucPdkWmZpJex8b2T-0LlQc7qwWdR)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGaKbXCYBCjlQ6f60-vU4xT8gDGL52r5iK47W3BJu46smJbwnyiq5lqBNkk4Nivoeh3otJvnkX2eiADuIP18bKqLsHIyhmCgT_kcb-OVgAzA7h4F-UBAWMACEZWiCPBllTLEI-DKDwDEaFQTjyzgF_RvQ==)\n[