{"step_index":58,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T22:45:07Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-17T04:15:07+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-17T04:15:13+05:30\nThe search for \"github \"image to video\" \"segment\" \"animation\" objects python\" returned the following summary:\nFor image-to-video animation tasks involving object segmentation and Python, several powerful GitHub repositories and tools are available. These projects generally combine segmentation models (like **SAM/SAM 2**) with video generation or animation frameworks.\n\n### Recommended GitHub Repositories & Tools\n\n*   **[PhysGen](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFAClooWf2bFZsaNfEgq_iN7o3gv8tDkEPVaYE_ndGR-jHFQkPG3JJuEhBiH5xqQjuVvxtOJN2bo2rWMuCBUYVkYoChVNxYeqNhCjHBEB1uOhZfldiyaDJe6HI=):** A research project focused on physics-grounded image-to-video generation. It uses **Grounded-Segment-Anything** to isolate foreground objects and apply physics-based animation (via Pymunk) before rendering with diffusion models[1].\n*   **[Tracking-Anything-with-DEVA](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_11ze8varDknAs_839-T9DccMI3iMIkNrRJmv53CSGoDSySTIGO4vIj1akZs5Of_31_oZtAqz9403WwU2IbrA93IAgKjRBBMb2AO0ghG8MuKeHo4APMEUMeYgsu5rBCdU97zKGadDZFQ=):** Excellent for projects requiring precise object tracking and segmentation in videos. It builds on the Segment Anything Model (SAM) and is ideal if your workflow requires segmenting objects across multiple frames for consistent animation[2].\n*   **[Nano Cinema AI Video Studio](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGfGYMnq3G5bPqG5sw6gTnQTpCrQCfqscP7TFnvqH7BXxc4HrUeZ5Uo57VC9BCtlpfheWFs7cYrxcZoKFWqz2kDoOG6oOLzdHW6S10PfDEKZQu1oZhU5kZf-9dEAFkAoN5oh2BEb8L0jPMRjxs=):** An all-in-one local pipeline that orchestrates various models (including LTX-Video) for cinematic video production. It includes logic for scene splitting and composition, which is useful for object-focused video workflows[3].\n*   **[Sketch2Motion](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF0-z4eVyC_4mUWdv_A9f1aIoaTWp6UlyyiWgFG6RBp9o0GIJFyBexf2E15QRpC1KVL9avKJQWvyRGqlYxQRouy8dcKdde1yAxMvREj5lP4oEUQLYdyoUOiU-8cwQ7X):** A tool specifically designed to convert static images/sketches into animated drawing videos using vector graphics and the Manim animation engine[4].\n*   **[MediaPipe (Google)](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGh0-NmhAuEoey-6i_D7tIV4Aay5hl52z3YBg1Dv1Bj25qhjxUpzT3MSCghFQadNMcUpnIvFldOCVZO7R1x6O7meUcOn3mF-djavC6Uq7iq9Rn7OFjbr8DJFzXHym2BQCXw_UEYQREYBJWV43xYsVZWoD6xHoVMq_jK5FBkLDDNratoWPZ6GvZp2Jqm5pJF_WJayPxaPh0E9ONNKgk6jrKtoWZKbo9P):** Offers a lightweight \"Image Segmenter\" API in Python. While more fundamental than a full animation suite, it is highly efficient for real-time applications where you need to isolate objects before passing them to an animation engine[5].\n\n### Core Technologies to Look For\nWhen searching GitHub for these capabilities, look for repositories that combine these specific Python libraries:\n*   **Segmentation:** `segment-anything` (SAM/SAM 2), `YOLOv8` (for fast object detection/segmentation), or `MediaPipe`.\n*   **Animation/Video Generation:** `AnimateDiff`, `ComfyUI` (which acts as a hub for many of these nodes)[6][7], and `FFmpeg` for video processing and rendering[3][4].\n*   **Control:** Projects mentioning \"ControlNet\" or \"Pose-driven animation\" are often the best for ensuring that specific objects move in the way you intend rather than just generating random motion[8][6].\n\n**Tip:** If you are building a custom pipeline, **ComfyUI** is currently the industry-standard \"no-code/low-code\" framework on GitHub for chaining these tasks—you can install specialized nodes for SAM segmentation and link them directly to image-to-video models like CogVideoX or LTX-Video[6][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFAClooWf2bFZsaNfEgq_iN7o3gv8tDkEPVaYE_ndGR-jHFQkPG3JJuEhBiH5xqQjuVvxtOJN2bo2rWMuCBUYVkYoChVNxYeqNhCjHBEB1uOhZfldiyaDJe6HI=)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_11ze8varDknAs_839-T9DccMI3iMIkNrRJmv53CSGoDSySTIGO4vIj1akZs5Of_31_oZtAqz9403WwU2IbrA93IAgKjRBBMb2AO0ghG8MuKeHo4APMEUMeYgsu5rBCdU97zKGadDZFQ=)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGfGYMnq3G5bPqG5sw6gTnQTpCrQCfqscP7TFnvqH7BXxc4HrUeZ5Uo57VC9BCtlpfheWFs7cYrxcZoKFWqz2kDoOG6oOLzdHW6S10PfDEKZQu1oZhU5kZf-9dEAFkAoN5oh2BEb8L0jPMRjxs=)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF0-z4eVyC_4mUWdv_A9f1aIoaTWp6UlyyiWgFG6RBp9o0GIJFyBexf2E15QRpC1KVL9avKJQWvyRGqlYxQRouy8dcKdde1yAxMvREj5lP4oEUQLYdyoUOiU-8cwQ7X)\n[5] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGh0-NmhAuEoey-6i_D7tIV4Aay5hl52z3YBg1Dv1Bj25qhjxUpzT3MSCghFQadNMcUpnIvFldOCVZO7R1x6O7meUcOn3mF-djavC6Uq7iq9Rn7OFjbr8DJFzXHym2BQCXw_UEYQREYBJWV43xYsVZWoD6xHoVMq_jK5FBkLDDNratoWPZ6GvZp2Jqm5pJF_WJayPxaPh0E9ONNKgk6jrKtoWZKbo9P)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFERLeukSNdPRDzM1Aey8p9XRbQLaBlzf8rVWx_N-w1kD_BOgHwtG265DogMxmEZm3uIygVgX7Ex4GQDRaNxnH2xbgRzrQwNtON7E-h2fQFicVGX6pQuHVOuFRfeBdDu2l6iODEqSUjIHVkfGisitFbg9W5RsIL)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG-2mVdEDj9H_cXQmyR0xyHqEsHmpJGHH5lOwG6w7scsusOgx64hmCt0ThF3BMy4bkVGukij68MZmsvCsYD3y6mH-a1zjyJVfsg1CrERlMmK1xQe1kxTsrsKtxuCd_ysTj2WgzotJzZnED5DaFCumQ4PRG-G7a1p6o1H1Z_njXvK2tOFgV4yoWIdTEZUQGa4eUuH5ko780a15na_kYWtEuYt_6VnaTUrfVN6MLYVmYIqqsW5Mji2CzTq-fu_26-dd6j8iEBvlKgXA==)\n[8] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFlgZeojQAxSgWeW53nikgeTHa2i06glhvy5vkD5hqdYYcsgSd26ZNJZzAmS-1BQKpdAs6fYnrY8OEVbFaru_mW2WLHOwX9gp7qnQO2ZEx0Km3_HMq4i50p5GbRZ9dx8_V_Mco=)"}
