{"step_index":60,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T22:45:16Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-17T04:15:16+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-17T04:15:20+05:30\nThe search for \"\"Sketch2Motion\" github OR \"PhysGen\" github\" returned the following summary:\nBelow are the GitHub repositories and project details for **Sketch2Motion** and **PhysGen**.\n\n### **1. Sketch2Motion**\nThere are two distinct projects often referred to by this name:\n\n*   **Sketch2Motion (Animation Tool):** A tool to convert photos or sketches into animated MP4 videos using Manim.\n    *   **GitHub Repository:** [leeyeel/Sketch2Motion](https://github.com/leeyeel/sketch2motion)\n    *   **Description:** This project takes a doodle or photo, converts it into an SVG vector graphic, and renders it into a smooth drawing animation. It includes a Gradio web interface and allows for customizable animation styles and parameters[1][2].\n*   **Sketch2Motion (Research - Skeleton Optimization):** A research project titled *\"Sketch2Motion: Text-driven 2D Sketch to 3D Animation via Diffusion-guided Skeleton Optimization.\"*\n    *   **Details:** This framework uses diffusion models and skeleton optimization to animate 2D sketches. It is associated with researchers Gaurav Rai and Ojaswa Sharma[3][4]. You can find project pages and academic publications via ResearchGate or the authors' personal pages, though the code is often linked within their specific research repository collections[5][4][6].\n\n---\n\n### **2. PhysGen**\nThere are also two prominent projects under the name **PhysGen**:\n\n*   **PhysGen (Rigid-Body Physics-Grounded Image-to-Video Generation):**\n    *   **GitHub Repository:** [stevenlsw/physgen](https://github.com/stevenlsw/physgen)\n    *   **Description:** This project (ECCV 2024) focuses on image-to-video generation that is physically plausible. It integrates model-based physical simulation with data-driven video generation to produce videos where objects behave realistically according to forces and torques[7][8][9].\n*   **PhysGen (Physically Grounded 3D Shape Generation):**\n    *   **GitHub Repository:** [kasvii/PhysGen](https://github.com/kasvii/PhysGen)\n    *   **Description:** A framework (CVPR 2026) for industrial design that models geometry and physical properties in a shared latent space to generate 3D shapes that are both aesthetically and physically valid (e.g., aerodynamic cars)[10][11].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF9mz4n6vVHDjji2tG6g_KyGVu9jAD80q4De-bxHBCnEDCelpKuMafPsvjFwxCHgQU2DOoeWYu72u3HYyzigrhM1azKWVifBVMSfSDVXqCEQtmeM_M8qIvzWT41Lic=)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF96m0ITT5EBHGQ_UZwiJxs22lZ0hLcSJFyB1_qsmgb_pQFzHmk3sKwgALN0pg0pAweYETp4LLmaEpsEkkWEpSP_i_T0WK_kfz1nkqCflRo)\n[3] [huggingface.co](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHw7qfx2U4Z4Mo_JCL6YBtZAWQxX_ENU9bGUOh9ucXERhxpMfm3xMxV8EbprutR6V1kzZoaXRcW5cs8aw65pJmSrXOjwYj8Jb7z_oJfkLsTVBfyfzfcumzRE3A9Tdk=)\n[4] [github.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHK5uO252Ok3aWgVWTkghRcoMqPCChoyQJHyoRxXj9iPRM5VkJ1Gresxd1RHi23fVmXkKT1n6ybQXEbx0yHoeTlf0qwzDVcAN3UhwwmZSdlgWaCBc_wSQ==)\n[5] [researchgate.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE8H5WfOh9drzXMvDXayPmQqAAkjuwNqhMWdivaECGY0buUij8MIQlG5zV60-cnIDLD38hVz92INbJfrJ3-cW9AGZ13Qr137om7hLgfKqc7IcfByYMbylhOeNajykYp0vPuLZgpZrXgxlQqMKxjGEdhBIap7OA_TQzGPpELTml2_JRruBZ-7k4Vft9HAJS_eovHq-TsoLyFmxTmSoxYrDOSga62A8DaxR2S_k720fsbz7iFNlwIPm30fv3ily4kxemWzNMMhjCg)\n[6] [researchgate.net](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEWdvYRPB88N8zbF6sg_t55nOcEmid8vkKvK-xyCrt0kRGppTkBCpeq_mLBMIEYFz5fUdnlqkQI7rvLVzcdMPUzG308a8kDqhihAnSESenW-PdBfsCV4jedys0LDeGXbbvcInay5gZICRqhlFnCaHCuSz1PcoTaRa4VjNl3fQzNfNjKNdaYDF5WyNAjW7ofJnEcXBDA9dICzjVn7NiT5NSmCWs=)\n[7] [github.com](h