{"step_index":74,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T22:45:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-17T04:15:51+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-17T04:15:54+05:30\nThe search for \"site:github.com \"popup\" (\"segmentation\" OR \"segment\") \"animation\"\" returned the following summary:\nFor search queries on GitHub involving \"popup,\" \"segmentation/segment,\" and \"animation,\" the results primarily point to curated lists of iOS animation libraries and UI components[1][2][3][4].\n\n### Key Findings\n*   **Curated Lists (Awesome Repos):** Large repositories like `onmyway133/awesome-ios-animation` and `ilyi1116/awesome-ios-ui-1` serve as hubs[1][4]. These lists categorize components—including **Popups** and **Segmented Controls**—that feature custom animations[1][3][4].\n*   **Specific Components & Examples:**\n    *   **Segmented Controls:** Repositories often highlight `PinterestSegment`, which is noted for its \"Pinterest-like\" masking animation[3][4][5], and `SJFluidSegmentedControl` for interactive animations[3][4].\n    *   **Popups/Menus:** Components like `FTPopOverMenu_Swift` (a pop-over menu) and `PopMenu` (a popup-style action sheet) are frequently referenced for their animation capabilities[5].\n    *   **Sliders:** Some components, such as `Fluid Slider`, combine these concepts by providing a \"popup bubble\" animation to display values on a slider[4].\n*   **General Web/HTML Snippets:** Occasionally, you may find smaller, individual project snippets—such as an \"animated cat loader\" that uses segments and gradients to create an animation[6].\n\nIf you are looking for a specific codebase, you may want to refine your search by adding the programming language (e.g., `Swift`, `JavaScript`, or `CSS`) to narrow down the results from these general \"awesome\" lists.\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE_gs4T47Z060OwMA4FHCk429c_LLmvqC_-E2Er20g5vJYxkJB3M6eE99J3SzF8x